# CLI (`@dimah-s3/cli`)

Scaffold only — no dimah-s3 business logic. Two phases, never mixed: **resolve** (flags + prompts → `CreateConfig`) then **steps** (all filesystem writes). `create/config.ts` owns every prompt; `create/pipeline.ts` runs `createSteps` and prints next steps.

Steps implement `CreateStep` (`create/step.ts`): `id`, `title`, `enabled`, `recoverable`, `run(ctx, report)`. The runner owns output (spinner on TTY, plain lines otherwise) — never call Clack `tasks()` (leaks the spinner on throw). Rollback only removes a target dir the run created.

Templates SSOT: `templates/<id>/` + `templates/catalog.json` (not a workspace member). Build snapshots into `dist/templates/` (pins `@dimah-s3/*`, rejects `catalog:` / `workspace:*`, renames `.gitignore` → `_gitignore`).

New template → catalog entry + folder. New create option → flag + `CreateConfig` field + a step in `createSteps`. Do not hand-edit `dist/templates/`.

